WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:02.949
We live in a society.

00:00:02.949 --> 00:00:08.029
That much is true in the SCP Foundation’s
native universe, or any others.

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:12.619
But whenever you live in a society, there
is always the threat that someone with malicious

00:00:12.619 --> 00:00:17.630
intent will come and tear your carefully-constructed
society down.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:24.380
People like, say, the Joker, the iconic, terrifying,
and darkly hilarious Clown Prince of Crime

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.690
from the world of DC Comics.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:31.791
The Joker has been causing chaos in the worlds
of comics, cartoons, movies, TV Shows, and

00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:38.070
video games for almost a century, from Romero
to Nicholson to Hamill to Ledger to Phoenix,

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.750
and when he’s not duking it out with the
Dark Knight, he’s doing everything he can

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:47.420
to prove that the world is only one bad day
away from total pandemonium.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:52.750
And to that end, he regularly allies with
anomalous entities, people, and groups.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.730
That’s more than enough to put him in the
sights of the SCP Foundation.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:02.010
So today, we’re using the trusty Anom-O-Tron
6000 - our state-of-the-art simulation computer,

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:06.860
made through proprietary anomalous means - to
see how exactly a tussle with the Joker might

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:07.860
go.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:11.670
And if there’s one thing we know about this
grease-painted gangster, it’s that regardless

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:16.830
of where he pops up, he always needs a mentally
ill dude with an incredibly tragic backstory

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:20.450
and a bunch of special skills and gadgets
to take him down.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:24.049
Enter the SCP Foundation’s very own Dr.
Jack Bright.

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:28.869
It’s an unstoppable chaotic force Vs an
immovable chaotic object.

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:29.869
But who will win?

00:01:29.869 --> 00:01:32.590
Let’s crank up the machine and find out!

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.810
It was pandemonium over at Site-19.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:39.880
Bodies littered the ground, the walls were
perforated with bullet holes.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:43.200
Several anomalies had been stolen, and another
several had escaped.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.700
It was one of those worst-case scenario type
situations.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.869
And naturally, this meant a guaranteed stressful
morning for the unimitable Site Director,

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:57.080
Dr. Bright, who already had enough on his
plate trying to organize the annual SCP Foundation

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.170
Christmas party.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:03.979
He entered the main hall, where a heated confrontation
between Foundation Agents and a group of heavily-armed

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:06.090
interlopers had taken place.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.920
Jack was flanked on both sides by several
Mobile Task Force operatives who’d been

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.920
dispatched to help fight off these foes, but
by the time they’d arrived, the intruders

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.500
had already disappeared.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.520
Dr. Bright shook his head and tutted, surveying
the room.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.680
There were at least twenty or thirty bodies,
considerable property damage, and even green

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:30.470
graffiti spraypainted onto the walls, depicting
mostly crude symbols like evil smiley faces,

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:36.790
Anarchy A’s, the Stussy S, and some words
we need to blur out, because SCP Explained

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:38.380
is a family show.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:42.880
In some regards, it had all the hallmarks
of a typical Chaos Insurgency raid: A group

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:48.130
of heavily-armed operatives steaming in, guns
blazing, indulging in a little smash and grab,

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.270
and leaving a trail of Foundation operative
blood on the way out.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:56.150
But there were certain details here that gave
Dr. Bright pause, before resetting the typical

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:00.519
“X Days Since Chaos Insurgency Attack”
on the break room whiteboard.

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:05.460
Dr. Bright waded forward into the carnage,
stepping delicately around multiple bodies

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.460
on the ground.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.820
There were many of those strange little wind-up
chattering teeth, producing tinny laughter

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:13.130
from their tiny voice boxes.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:18.150
There was a funny smell lingering in the air,
almost like circus peanuts and cotton candy.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:23.269
But the weirdest of all was what had happened
to the bodies of the Foundation operatives

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:29.510
themselves: All had pale faces, wide, staring
eyes, and bright red grins.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:33.900
Why had so many of them died bearing such
grotesque smiles?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.620
Was this some new anomalous entity or weapon
that Bright had never even heard of?

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:42.540
When the Chaos Insurgency discovered an anomaly
before the Foundation, it never boded well

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.540
for anyone.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:48.370
That’s when Dr. Bright heard something from
one of the bodies on the ground: A deep, hacking

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.659
cough.

00:03:49.659 --> 00:03:53.560
Bright immediately ran over to the body in
question: It was a junior researcher who’d

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:58.860
had the presence of mind to put on a gas mask
and play possum as soon as the attack began,

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:03.549
leaving him the only survivor and eyewitness
to the account, as the interlopers had been

00:04:03.549 --> 00:04:06.849
smart enough to kill all the cameras before
the attack began.

00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:11.800
“Phew, thank 343 somebody survived this
catastrophe,” Dr. Bright said, wiping some

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:12.800
sweat from his brow.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.349
“What the heck happened here, kid?”

00:04:14.349 --> 00:04:19.410
The junior researcher slid off his gas mask,
revealing his trembling, tear-streaked face.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:22.470
It took him a moment of steadying himself
to speak.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.089
“I’ve never seen anything like this.

00:04:25.089 --> 00:04:29.849
It was a Chaos Insurgency raid, I recognized
all the uniforms from those seminars we needed

00:04:29.849 --> 00:04:30.849
to take in orientation.

00:04:30.849 --> 00:04:33.009
But... but there was this one guy with them.

00:04:33.009 --> 00:04:35.330
I’ve never seen anything like it.”

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.699
“What kind of guy are we talking about here?”

00:04:37.699 --> 00:04:38.900
Bright asked.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:39.900
“He...

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:44.349
He had a white face, like a clown, with these
big, red lips and green hair.

00:04:44.349 --> 00:04:46.729
And he wore a purple suit.

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:47.780
And that laugh.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.770
God, I’m never gonna forget that laugh...

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.979
When he came in, he released some kind of
toxin.

00:04:51.979 --> 00:04:56.909
I saw everyone who got enveloped by the cloud
start laughing like him - Not happy laughing,

00:04:56.909 --> 00:04:58.729
laughing like it hurt, but they couldn’t
stop.

00:04:58.729 --> 00:05:02.849
I was able to put on my gas mask just in time,
but then the Chaos Insurgency guys with him

00:05:02.849 --> 00:05:04.319
opened fire.

00:05:04.319 --> 00:05:05.539
It was ten minutes of hell.

00:05:05.539 --> 00:05:06.539
And then...

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:07.999
They were all just gone.”

00:05:07.999 --> 00:05:12.110
And with that, the junior researcher passed
out from the stress of recalling his traumatic

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:13.110
incident.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:16.590
Bright ordered some of his subordinates to
cart the kid off to the medical ward while

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:19.180
they straightened the rest of this madness
out.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:24.300
So the Chaos Insurgency had found themselves
a new star operative - or some new maniac

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.389
is out there calling the shots now.

00:05:26.389 --> 00:05:28.839
Either way, bad news bears.

00:05:28.839 --> 00:05:33.340
Dr. Bright narrowed his eyes pensively and
said, “I think a man who calls himself The

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:35.080
Joker was behind this attack.”

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:39.389
“What makes you think this, Doctor?” asked
Sergeant Richards, an MTF Officer.

00:05:39.389 --> 00:05:43.889
“The graffiti is definitely a pretty strong
clue,” Bright replied.

00:05:43.889 --> 00:05:48.259
On the wall to the left of Bright and Richards
were the words, “I WAS BEHIND THIS - SIGNED,

00:05:48.259 --> 00:05:49.259
THE JOKER.

00:05:49.259 --> 00:05:50.259
P.S.

00:05:50.259 --> 00:05:51.259
HA HA HA!”

00:05:51.259 --> 00:05:54.619
etched out in that same garish, green spray
paint.

00:05:54.619 --> 00:05:59.259
As with any attack on the SCP Foundation’s
primary base, Dr. Bright needed to perform

00:05:59.259 --> 00:06:04.960
a debrief with O5-1, the leader of the O5
Council, and discuss the plans for how they

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.219
want to deal with this new “Joker” fellow
that seems to be buddy-buddy with the Chaos

00:06:09.219 --> 00:06:10.610
Insurgency now.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:15.810
Dr. Bright sat at the end of a frankly unnecessarily
long meeting table, with a live video feed

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:20.349
to O5-1’s undisclosed secure location on
the other end.

00:06:20.349 --> 00:06:22.789
But things were about to get a whole lot worse.

00:06:22.789 --> 00:06:27.909
Because as Dr. Bright explained the situation
to O5-1, the last thing he expected in response

00:06:27.909 --> 00:06:31.699
was for the man to say, “Oh god, him again?”

00:06:31.699 --> 00:06:37.669
As it turned out, in the anxiety-inducing
spiel that Dr. Bright would receive from O5-1,

00:06:37.669 --> 00:06:42.740
this Joker had really been making a name for
himself in the SCP Foundation’s bad books.

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:47.610
He’d done several jobs with the Chaos Insurgency,
but that was apparently only the start of

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:52.370
his work with the Foundation’s various most
maligned Groups of Interest.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:55.879
Foundation informants have reported that the
Joker - The moniker they’d need to stick

00:06:55.879 --> 00:07:00.289
with, since seemingly nobody knows the guy’s
true name - had sold several of the high-value

00:07:00.289 --> 00:07:04.849
anomalies he’d collected with the Chaos
Insurgency to the heartless moneymen at Marshall,

00:07:04.849 --> 00:07:09.789
Carter, and Dark Ltd., and he’d been using
the resulting capital to fund himself an increasingly

00:07:09.789 --> 00:07:12.680
large and dangerous criminal empire.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.270
But it didn’t stop there.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:19.059
Given the Joker’s silly yet deadly clown
theme, he’d been using his ill-gotten gains

00:07:19.059 --> 00:07:22.259
to purchase whimsical weaponry from the Wondertainment
Corporation.

00:07:22.259 --> 00:07:27.129
And to give him plenty of anomalous manpower,
he’d been headhunting the various super-powered

00:07:27.129 --> 00:07:31.610
freaks working at Herman Fuller’s Circus
of the Disquieting, whom he lured over with

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:36.639
both higher pay, and comprehensive company
dental insurance to make sure those big, evil

00:07:36.639 --> 00:07:39.120
smiles were full of pearly whites.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.199
Nobody knew what his end goal was, but it
was clear that the Joker was now an established

00:07:43.199 --> 00:07:48.029
power player among the deluge of dangerous
Groups of Interest out there, at the expense

00:07:48.029 --> 00:07:51.139
of many, many Foundation lives.

00:07:51.139 --> 00:07:52.139
“So...

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:53.740
What are we gonna do about him?”

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:54.770
Dr. Bright asked.

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:58.650
“Send over the boys from Red Right Hand
to give him the JFK special?”

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:01.729
“Don’t you think we’ve already tried
that approach, Jack?

00:08:01.729 --> 00:08:07.699
Please, don’t insult my intelligence with
such an obvious suggestion,” O5-1 replied.

00:08:07.699 --> 00:08:12.439
“We’ve sent numerous hit squads to take
him out, but he always seems to be one step

00:08:12.439 --> 00:08:13.439
ahead.

00:08:13.439 --> 00:08:16.610
The last one got a tip-off that he’d be
hiding in a penthouse apartment in Gotham

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:19.529
City - some absolute toilet bowl of a town.

00:08:19.529 --> 00:08:23.020
But when the team arrived, all they saw was
a comically large gift-wrapped present with

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:26.559
a note saying, ‘For the SCP Foundation.

00:08:26.559 --> 00:08:29.379
Lots of love, Mister J.’”

00:08:29.379 --> 00:08:34.469
“Well, that’s not so bad,” Dr. Bright
started to say, before O5-1 cut him off with:

00:08:34.469 --> 00:08:37.680
“Turned out the present was filled with
highly-pressurized napalm.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:41.459
Next time we saw that team, well, let’s
just say that the Joker saved us the standard

00:08:41.459 --> 00:08:44.580
cremation costs for employee fatalities.”

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.850
“Oh,” Dr. Bright replied.

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:49.450
“Yeah, that’s pretty bad, actually.”

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:53.029
O5-1 told him that the solution was exceedingly
simple.

00:08:53.029 --> 00:08:57.079
To defeat a dangerous prankster, you need
to send a dangerous prankster after them.

00:08:57.079 --> 00:09:00.810
Dr. Bright would be the perfect candidate
to track down and take down the Joker in the

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:06.360
name of the SCP Foundation, but of course,
Jack had one advantage that the Joker didn’t:

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:08.510
Jack was pretty much impossible to kill.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:14.070
However, it wouldn’t stop this demented
clown from hurting him really, really bad.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:19.710
It was clear that the Joker somehow had a
mole inside the Foundation, which is why,

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:24.769
for maximum security, O5-1 decided to keep
this little mission purely between himself,

00:09:24.769 --> 00:09:28.980
Dr. Bright, and the Foundation spy that tipped
them off to the Joker’s current whereabouts:

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:34.060
A lair he’d constructed in an abandoned
amusement park in Gotham City.

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:38.959
Dr. Bright felt tempted to comment that maybe
this was a little too obvious, but decided

00:09:38.959 --> 00:09:43.779
to hold his tongue, because he didn’t feel
like getting chewed out by O5-1 again today.

00:09:43.779 --> 00:09:48.680
He would be flown out to Gotham City in a
classified Foundation helicopter so that he

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:51.750
could enter with as little fanfare as possible.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:55.930
From there, he would need to track down and
incapacitate or kill the Joker himself.

00:09:55.930 --> 00:10:00.740
It wouldn’t be an easy task, but at least
it would distract him from causing mischief

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:04.000
of his own at the SCP Foundation in the meantime.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:08.670
Dr. Bright soon found that they really weren’t
kidding about Gotham City: The place was a

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:09.670
dump.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:13.670
It was like the very worst parts of New York
and Chicago had a dirty, gothic baby full

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:16.389
of mobsters and flamboyant supervillains.

00:10:16.389 --> 00:10:19.860
A hotbed of malice, poverty, and unchecked
crime.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:23.230
The kind of place where you could probably
get shot while leaving the theater with your

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:27.670
wife and young son, even if you were some
kind of billionaire philanthropist.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:32.250
It was no surprise to Dr. Bright that a place
like this would produce a maniac like the

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.250
Joker.

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:37.170
He’d be eager to leave once the greasepainted
freak was defeated.

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:40.730
Rather than risking any flashy Foundation
vehicle that might draw too much attention

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:45.860
to himself, Dr. Bright simply took a cab to
the edge of the abandoned amusement park.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:50.470
It was a dark, dismal place, surrounded by
a thick mist that really contributed to a

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:52.420
general mood of foreboding.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:56.899
Dr. Bright could see figures moving in the
mist, so he lifted up his pair of Foundation

00:10:56.899 --> 00:11:01.220
binoculars, which would easily cleave through
the mist and get to the truth of the situation

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.220
beyond.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:05.290
And the situation was definitely less than
ideal.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.720
It was a hive of clownish activity on the
other side.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:13.420
Weirdly buff henchmen in clown makeup carried
large boxes - presumably filled with weapons

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:18.930
or stolen anomalous items - while other muscular
mutant clowns carrying assault rifles guarded

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:19.930
them.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:24.339
Just beyond them, there was a huge funhouse,
shaped like a giant clown’s head.

00:11:24.339 --> 00:11:28.899
Given the Joker’s general lack of subtlety,
Dr. Bright assumed - correctly, we might add

00:11:28.899 --> 00:11:33.730
- that this would be where the Clown Prince
of Crime would choose to hang his hat.

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:38.389
That’s where Bright would sneak in, club
him into unconsciousness with a Foundation-issued

00:11:38.389 --> 00:11:43.149
defensive baton, and then call in backup to
take the bothersome jester away.

00:11:43.149 --> 00:11:44.930
It was a perfect plan.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:48.980
Dr. Bright infiltrated the amusement park
and began to sneak through.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:53.230
Thankfully for him, he’d learned perfect
stealth from years of discretely putting buckets

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:57.850
full of water on top of the doors of some
of the SCP Foundation’s most distinguished

00:11:57.850 --> 00:11:58.920
operatives.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:02.790
This made it an absolute cakewalk for him
to slip in between the oafish freaks that

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:07.689
the Joker had hired straight from the greedy
anomalous ringmaster, Herman Fuller.

00:12:07.689 --> 00:12:12.199
As Bright drew closer and closer to the funhouse
where the Joker was most certainly lurking,

00:12:12.199 --> 00:12:16.649
he wondered why this had even been considered
such a challenge by members of the Foundation’s

00:12:16.649 --> 00:12:18.749
most well-trained mobile task forces.

00:12:18.749 --> 00:12:23.519
Unless, he thought with an internal chuckle,
this whole thing was some kind of ridiculous,

00:12:23.519 --> 00:12:24.620
elaborate trap.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:29.040
Though Dr. Bright didn’t get to finish that
thought because before the thought was done,

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:33.420
a muscular arm brought a blackjack down onto
the back of Bright’s head, knocking him

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.019
unconscious.

00:12:35.019 --> 00:12:39.240
When Dr. Bright awoke - his ego more bruised
than his head, thankfully - he was tied up

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:43.050
at the bottom of a throne as extravagant as
it was strange.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:48.560
Atop this throne sat the Joker himself, eating
from a plate of Little Caesars’ Crazy Bread,

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:53.450
though to a man as demented as the Joker,
Crazy Bread was just considered Normal Bread.

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:58.730
Bright shifted on the ground slightly, and
saw a familiar yet strange face behind him,

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:01.610
wielding the blackjack that had laid him out
not long ago.

00:13:01.610 --> 00:13:07.339
It was a classic person of interest: The Man
with the Upside Down Face, also known as Manny,

00:13:07.339 --> 00:13:11.939
who’d been head recruiter at the Circus
of the Disquieting, and Herman Fuller’s

00:13:11.939 --> 00:13:14.980
right-hand man... with an upside down face.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:19.790
Manny was an utterly ruthless figure, not
above intimidation, violence, and kidnapping

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:22.200
to achieve the goals of his employers.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:26.560
It only made sense he’d work for the Joker
- it gave him a chance to continue doing what

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:27.560
he did best.

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:31.490
Jack’s thoughts were interrupted by a cackle
from the man of the hour.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:39.430
“Well, well, well, if it isn’t Dr. Jack
Bright - Jack of all trades, master of getting

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:41.110
captured,” he gloated.

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:44.790
“So delighted to finally be making your
acquaintance!

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:48.579
The ones they’ve been sending so far have
been so darn boring.

00:13:48.579 --> 00:13:52.800
It’s why I’ve been sending them back,
extra crispy!”

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.410
Dr. Bright struggled against his bindings,
to no avail.

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:58.100
“How do you know my name, you gaudy freak?”

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.290
Jack asked.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:03.910
This got another laugh out of the Joker, who
rose up from his throne and began dismounting,

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:08.570
holding an ornate walking cane with a tiny
gold version of his own face on it for a handle.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:10.080
This guy really had a knack for presentation.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:15.790
“I know a lot about you, Jack, especially
not to lay a hand on that pretty necklace

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:16.790
of yours,” the Joker said.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:21.910
“But in the wise words of the great Shania
Twain, that don’t impress me much.

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:27.120
No, Jack, what I find so interesting about
you is the fact you seem to be the only one

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:31.459
working for those Killjoys at the SCP Foundation
who has a sense of humor!”

00:14:31.459 --> 00:14:33.899
The Joker was standing right in front of him
now.

00:14:33.899 --> 00:14:36.550
Jack was at eye level with his fancy black
brogues.

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:41.449
If only he could get out of his bindings,
Jack would complete the obnoxious clown’s

00:14:41.449 --> 00:14:43.949
look by giving him a big, red nose.

00:14:43.949 --> 00:14:48.319
But instead, the Joker looked at Manny, and
waved the upside-down-faced henchman away.

00:14:48.319 --> 00:14:51.470
As Manny left the room, the Joker produced
a long knife from his coat.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.559
Jack certainly didn’t like the look of that...

00:14:53.559 --> 00:14:58.160
...Until the Joker leaned over, cut through
Jack’s bindings, and helped him to his feet,

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.900
even brushing the dust off his lab coat.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:02.180
“I didn’t bring you here to die, Jack.

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:03.959
That’d be a waste of effort.

00:15:03.959 --> 00:15:08.940
I’d have just sent somebody to come shoot
you and bury your medallion in concrete,”

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:11.079
the Joker said, patting Jack on the back.

00:15:11.079 --> 00:15:17.800
“No, no, no, I want to offer you a job on
the ground floor of my new growing enterprise!

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.949
I’m looking for a team player.

00:15:19.949 --> 00:15:21.120
Someone with experience.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:26.000
And most importantly, someone who knows how
to take a joke.”

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.680
Dr. Bright was confused.

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:31.259
This wasn’t how he expected this to go at
all.

00:15:31.259 --> 00:15:33.459
“What exactly is this enterprise?”

00:15:33.459 --> 00:15:34.610
Dr. Bright asked.

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:37.949
“That’s simple, my good man,” the Joker
said.

00:15:37.949 --> 00:15:41.649
“I’m going to steal up all the anomalies
I can, and use them to make this world a little

00:15:41.649 --> 00:15:43.330
more interesting.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:49.759
All those other groups I’ve worked with,
including yours, are all too focused on consolidating

00:15:49.759 --> 00:15:51.269
power.

00:15:51.269 --> 00:15:57.139
Even the so-called Chaos Insurgency really
just wants order, their order.

00:15:57.139 --> 00:15:58.139
Me?

00:15:58.139 --> 00:16:01.810
I just want life to be a party; I don’t
need to be the host.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:07.800
And with enough anomalies, I can tear reality
a new one, and make everyone see the world

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.119
how I see it.

00:16:09.119 --> 00:16:10.740
It’s the ultimate prank!

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.170
The gag to end all gags!

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:18.410
And in this new world, Jack, nobody will tell
you what you’re not allowed to do!

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:23.579
You’ll finally be free - just like yours
truly!”

00:16:23.579 --> 00:16:25.300
Jack thought about it for a moment.

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:31.540
It was an undeniably exciting idea - Finally
working at a job that valued him for his unique

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:32.769
attributes.

00:16:32.769 --> 00:16:37.970
Being part of something that let him be himself,
rather than constantly scolding him for doing

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:39.990
what they perceived to be wrong.

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:42.230
Who gave them the right to decide, after all?

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:46.170
Dr. Bright could see the Joker’s mouth stretching
into a wide grin as he considered it.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:50.439
Could he really betray everything and everyone
to make the world a more comfortable place

00:16:50.439 --> 00:16:51.439
for himself?

00:16:51.439 --> 00:16:53.600
“Well, Jack?” the Joker asked.

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:55.160
“What’ll it be?”

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.990
Jack sighed and punched the Joker in his grinning
face.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.680
The clown staggered back, furious.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:03.149
He yelled, “So that’s how it’s gonna
be, huh?

00:17:03.149 --> 00:17:06.400
Okay, Jack, guess you’re just another sad
sack!”

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:10.140
Dr. Bright stepped forward to take another
swing, but the Joker grabbed at the false

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:11.689
flower on his lapel.

00:17:11.689 --> 00:17:16.860
The flower squirted a thin stream of highly-concentrated
acid at Dr. Bright, but the anomalous Foundation

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.510
researcher thought quickly.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:22.890
He grabbed and lifted up his indestructible
medallion, using it as a mini shield to block

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:23.980
the acid.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:28.779
It burnt his hand a little, but most of the
potentially devastating damage was deflected.

00:17:28.779 --> 00:17:32.480
As Bright continued running towards the Joker,
the clown pressed a button on the top of his

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:35.570
cane, causing the device to turn into a sword.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:39.710
As the Joker swung for him, Jack pulled out
his Foundation-issued defensive baton.

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:44.360
They clashed weapons with impressive speed
and ferocity, but the Joker undeniably had

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:47.250
a kind of vicious killer instinct that Dr.
Bright didn’t.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:51.480
Jack killed to live, the Joker killed for
the sheer fun of it.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:54.330
“Face it, Bright, you can't beat me!”

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:55.570
Joker yelled.

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:59.090
“I’m da Joker, baby!”

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:00.919
But gloating was a mistake.

00:18:00.919 --> 00:18:02.340
It gave Jack a window.

00:18:02.340 --> 00:18:05.830
While the Joker was midway through one of
his demented laughs, and their respective

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:10.120
weapons were locked into a mutual clash, Dr.
Bright punched the Joker in the throat with

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:11.430
his spare hand.

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:15.780
It broke the clown’s laugh off into a choking
splutter as he stumbled backwards.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:19.789
Seizing his opportunity, Jack kicked the Joker
in the chest and knocked him to the ground,

00:18:19.789 --> 00:18:21.860
clattering the cane sword from his hand.

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:22.860
“No fair!”

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:24.149
The Joker spluttered out.

00:18:24.149 --> 00:18:28.111
Dr. Bright reached into his coat to grab the
emergency handgun he brought with him, but

00:18:28.111 --> 00:18:29.240
it was too late.

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:33.230
The Joker, laying on his back, had already
pulled his own gun on Dr. Bright, and was

00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:35.040
aiming it right at him.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.490
The Joker didn’t hesitate.

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:38.530
He pulled the trigger - Bang!

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:42.870
As in, the word “Bang!” on a little flag
popped out of the wind of the Joker’s pistol.

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:46.450
Dr. Bright was bemused as the Joker just started
laughing again.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:50.880
This whole thing really was nothing more than
a big gag to this guy, wasn’t it?

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:53.530
“Sorry, Jack,” the Joker said, regaining
his voice.

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:55.130
“I couldn’t resist.”

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:59.360
Then, the Joker squeezed the trigger again,
causing the little flag to fire out with the

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:01.960
speed and force of a crossbow bolt.

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:06.620
Thankfully, Dr. Bright was able to dodge,
causing the flag to stick into his shoulder,

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:09.210
rather than his intended target, the heart.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.920
But Jack had had enough.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:14.800
The exhausted researcher pulled out his gun
and aimed it at the Joker’s head.

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:17.740
He was bringing this clown back to Site-19
cold.

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:19.990
The Joker still laughed, even at this.

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:22.950
He stuck out his tongue in a childish gesture
of spite.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:27.590
“I hate clowns,” Dr. Bright said, pulling
back the hammer and curling his finger around

00:19:27.590 --> 00:19:28.590
the trigger.

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:32.710
He was about to fire when a black-clad had
closed around his wrist.

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:36.010
Bright turned, baffled, to see Batman holding
his wrist.

00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:37.640
“Sorry, kid,” Batman said.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:40.730
“But I didn’t get into this game to let
anyone get shot.

00:19:40.730 --> 00:19:42.020
Not even him.”

00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:43.980
Bright was too confused to reply.

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:46.140
The Joker gave a performative sigh.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:50.870
“You always know how to ruin the fun, Bats,”
Joker groaned.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:54.840
Before Dr. Bright could formulate a reply,
Batman punched him in the face, knocking him

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:56.789
out cold for the second time today.

00:19:56.789 --> 00:20:01.770
When Dr. Bright came to, both Batman and the
Joker were gone to god knows where.

00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:04.290
Dr. Bright sighed, rubbing his aching head.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:07.250
He really should have taken the Joker’s
deal, shouldn’t he?

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:14.260
Now go check out “SCP-001 When Day Breaks
Dr Bright” and “SCP-682 VS Dr. Bright”

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:17.680
for more of the wacky adventures of Dr. Jack
Bright!

